 "headline": "On 200 labelled synthetic images, Drishyam at a 30% pixel cap found 0.47 of ground-truth boxes using 0.23 of the image's pixels, versus 0.55 for 20%-overlap 512-px tiling using 1.67: 0.85x its recall (95% CI 0.79-0.91, 0.73x with one-box-per-class boxes, 1.21x with as-specified mixed boxes) at 0.14x its pixels, which does not meet the 0.9x-at-0.3x hypothesis. It is 0.94x a single 1024-px downscale (95% CI 0.89-1.00, 0.50 at 0.25 of the pixels), 0.84x L1 tiling (0.55 at 0.50, the best grid) and 1.06x L2 tiling (0.44 at 0.06), and 0.91x L0 tiling when a match needs IoU >= 0.3 (95% CI 0.84-0.98, no contains-the-centre clause); its own boxes placed at random would score 0.04 (0.02 with IoU only)."
